<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Cross-District Trail to Dutchman Flat</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:257-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.160159" lon="-121.636767"><ele>1572.2</ele><name>Upper Three Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 100326940); confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; book_elev_ft: 5120; quote: map 58: UPPER 3 CREEK SNO-PARK 5120'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.160240" lon="-121.638620"><ele>1576.0</ele><name>Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16</name><desc>source: USFS trail 4084 THREE CREEKS LAKE XC, BMP 0.0 (on OSM NF 16 node 38583495, 5 m); confidence: high; pdf_page: 257; quote: From the sno-park ski a few yards south up Road 16 past the gate and turn right onto the Three Creek Lake Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.153620" lon="-121.636240"><ele>1667.7</ele><name>Warren's Loop junction</name><desc>source: USFS trail 4084 BMP 0.7 (end of its first segment); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 258; quote: At 0.7 mile, after a demanding short ascent, the trail meets Warren's Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.140530" lon="-121.644280"><ele>1787.5</ele><name>Near Jefferson View Shelter</name><desc>source: point of USFS trail 4084 nearest the shelter; shelter marked at 44.14078,-121.64504 in CalTopo 69BR and 44.141,-121.6451 in K3NT (67 m off the trail); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 258; quote: then 1.3 miles later passes near the Jefferson View Shelter in a large clearcut</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.124590" lon="-121.627030"><ele>1891.6</ele><name>Trail rejoins Road 16</name><desc>source: end of USFS trail 4084 (BMP 3.8) = OSM NF 16 node 38299531 (6 m); K3NT marker 'Jeff View Trail' 44.125,-121.627; confidence: high; pdf_page: 259; quote: From where the Three Creek Trail rejoins Road 16 after 4 miles</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.117960" lon="-121.628580"><ele>1930.8</ele><name>Trapper Meadow (Three Creek Meadow)</name><desc>source: OSM NF 16 node 3489644050 at K3NT marker 'Meadow TH' (11 m); Park Meadow Trail #96A (the book's Snow Creek return) leaves the road here; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 258; book_elev_ft: 6300; quote: map 58: TRAPPER MDW (3 CK MDW) 6300'; Road 16 0.5 from the trail; first view of Tam McArthur Rim is from Trapper Meadows, 1.5 miles below the lake</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.112125" lon="-121.622126"><ele>1945.6</ele><name>Road 370 junction (to Dutchman Flat)</name><desc>source: OSM node 2825719304 where NF 370 (way 357558084) leaves NF 16; 0.59 mi by road from wp 6 (map 0.6), 0.86 mi to the lake (map 0.9); confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; quote: map 58: Road 16 0.6 past Trapper Mdw to the 370 junction (TO DUTCHMAN FLAT), then 0.9 to the lake</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.048674" lon="-121.655352"><ele>2108.2</ele><name>Road 370 / 380 junction (6,880 ft), east of Moon Mtn</name><desc>source: OSM node 38483518 (NF 370 x NF 380); USGS topo labels it 370/380 J; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 267; book_elev_ft: 6880; quote: climbs through Happy Valley to the open slopes east of Broken Top at 6,880 feet (pdf 259); map 60: 6880' junction</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.034030" lon="-121.677070"><ele>2001.4</ele><name>Big Meadow west end (road 370)</name><desc>source: OSM node where Big Meadow Trail, Todd Ridge Trail and NF 370 meet; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 270; book_elev_ft: 6450; quote: then to the west end of Big Meadow and up the road to a blufftop viewpoint (PDF 270); Todd Ridge trail starts at the west end of Big Meadow (PDF 268)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.028440" lon="-121.665390"><ele>1974.7</ele><name>Little Meadow (Big Meadow Trail / Pete's Way)</name><desc>source: OSM junction of the nordic Big Meadow Trail (way 1467651000) and Pete's Way (way 662808005); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 268; book_elev_ft: 6450; quote: in 2.2 miles from the sno-park it enters Little Meadow ... Both Pete's Way and Swampy Lakes Trails exit from this meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.999772" lon="-121.663687"><ele>1935.4</ele><name>Dutchman Flat Sno-park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 559496151); confidence: high; pdf_page: 267; book_elev_ft: 6400; quote: map 60: DUTCHMAN FLAT NORDIC SNO-PARK 6400'</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Cross-District Trail to Dutchman Flat</name><desc>1. Upper Three Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16: osm (high), 0.11 mi | 2. Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16 -&gt; Warren's Loop junction: usfs-trail (high), 0.71 mi | 3. Warren's Loop junction -&gt; Near Jefferson View Shelter: usfs-trail (high), 1.44 mi | 4. Near Jefferson View Shelter -&gt; Trail rejoins Road 16: usfs-trail (high), 1.72 mi | 5. Trail rejoins Road 16 -&gt; Trapper Meadow (Three Creek Meadow): osm (high), 0.51 mi | 6. Trapper Meadow (Three Creek Meadow) -&gt; Road 370 junction (to Dutchman Flat): osm (high), 0.59 mi | 7. Road 370 junction (to Dutchman Flat) -&gt; Road 370 / 380 junction (6,880 ft), east of Moon Mtn: osm (medium), 9.74 mi | 8. Road 370 / 380 junction (6,880 ft), east of Moon Mtn -&gt; Big Meadow west end (road 370): osm (high), 1.93 mi | 9. Big Meadow west end (road 370) -&gt; Little Meadow (Big Meadow Trail / Pete's Way): osm (high), 0.91 mi | 10. Little Meadow (Big Meadow Trail / Pete's Way) -&gt; Dutchman Flat Sno-park: osm (high), 2.57 mi</desc>
